# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local infrastructure state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Named Docker volumes live in the Docker VM, not the working tree, so nothing here is
# strictly required. These entries exist so that a developer who switches the compose
# volumes to bind mounts (a common "let me look at the WAL" move) does not commit a
# PostgreSQL data directory or a Keycloak H2 file by accident.
infra/data/
infra/volumes/
infra/postgres-data/
infra/keycloak-data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db-journal
docker-compose.override.yml

